Feature: ACH Transfer Functionality\n\n  Scenario: ACH Transfer Confirmation Details\n    Given the User is logged in\n    And the User is on the ACH transfer section\n    And valid transfer details are entered and submitted\n    When the User submits the transfer\n    Then a confirmation message displays correct transfer details including account number, routing number, amount, and date\n\n  Scenario: ACH Transfer Section Accessibility\n    Given the User is logged in\n    When the User attempts to access the ACH transfer section with keyboard navigation\n    Then the section is accessible via keyboard\n    And the screen reader reads all elements correctly\n\n  Scenario Outline: Invalid ACH Transfer Details\n    Given the User is logged in\n    And the User is on the ACH transfer section\n    When the User enters <invalid_input>\n    Then an error message is displayed for the invalid input\n\n    Examples:\n      | invalid_input             |\n      | invalid account number    |\n      | invalid routing number    |\n      | negative transfer amount  |\n      | past transfer date        |\n\n  Scenario: Submit ACH Transfer\n    Given the User is logged in\n    And the User is on the ACH transfer section\n    And valid transfer details are entered\n    When the User clicks on the 'Submit' button\n    Then the transfer is submitted\n    And a confirmation message is displayed indicating successful transfer initiation\n\n  Scenario: Input ACH Transfer Details\n    Given the User is logged in\n    And the User is on the ACH transfer section\n    When the User enters a valid account number\n    And the User enters a valid routing number\n    And the User enters a transfer amount\n    And the User enters a transfer date\n    Then each input is accepted